[32m+[m[32m## Error Tracking & Logging (Chunk 12)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mChunk 12 adds **production-grade observability** so you can see what users are experiencing (Sentry), what the API is doing (Axiom logs), and basic traffic analytics (Plausible).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Sentry (Frontend: Cloudflare Pages + Next.js)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Install/config:** Sentry Next.js SDK added via the Sentry wizard in `web/`.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **DSN:** `NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN` is stored in Cloudflare Pages **Secrets/Variables** (and can exist locally in `web/.env.local`).[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Test page:** `/sentry-test` provides a “Trigger Error” button that throws an error to confirm capture.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Build note:** Source maps/releases require a Sentry auth token for the build step. If not set, Sentry still captures errors, but source map upload/release creation is skipped.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Sentry (API: Cloudflare Workers + Hono)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Worker DSN:** `SENTRY_DSN` is stored as a Worker secret.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Test endpoint:** `GET /__sentry-test` intentionally throws a server error so you can confirm it appears in the Sentry **Issues** dashboard.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Axiom (API Logging)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Dataset:** `newchums-api` dataset created in Axiom.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Token:** An Axiom ingest token is generated and stored as `AXIOM_TOKEN` (secret).[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Routing:** The API sends structured logs to Axiom with a request id, path, status, and duration.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Test endpoint:** `GET /__log-test` writes a test log event and returns `{ ok: true }`.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Plausible (Frontend Analytics)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Site:** `newchums.com` site created in Plausible.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Domain env:** `NEXT_PUBLIC_PLAUSIBLE_DOMAIN=newchums.com` is set in Cloudflare Pages variables and used by the layout script loader.[m
